WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.560
Stir a spoonful of salt
into a glass of water.

2
00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:05.390
The crystals vanish.

3
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.280
Pour in oil, and it refuses to mix.

4
00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:10.980
It sits on top, in its own layer.

5
00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:14.980
A typical cell is about
70 per cent water by mass.

6
00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.930
Most reactions of life
happen dissolved in it.

7
00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:22.530
So why does salt vanish into
water, while oil stays apart?

8
00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:26.790
In this mission, you'll find out why a
water molecule has a slightly negative

9
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:29.230
end and a slightly positive end.

10
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.970
Then you'll see water molecules
link up by hydrogen bonds:

11
00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:36.210
each one weak, millions strong together.

12
00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:41.480
Your mission: find out why salt vanishes
into water while oil floats apart.
